Z||000014||KnightRyder31||07-19-2000||11:36 AM||||Man!!! I love that 426ci HEMI!! I've drivin a 1970 Dodge Challenger R/T with that engine. Damn!!! That SOB moved!!! ||||reg||1
Z||000015||triker||07-19-2000||12:49 PM||||The 396 and 454 share the same casting as do the 350 and 400.  The 396-454 is a lot bigger and a lot heavier.  I don't think the 'big block' would make a very practical swap for the Fiero.  I did a 350 to 396 swap in a 76 pickup and had to put coil over shocks in it to bring the ride back to where it was with the 350.  The 400 is what most of the circle track racers are using around here and would probably be as much engine as anyone would want in thier Fiero. ||||reg||1
Z||000016||Child Of Rod||07-19-2000||11:37 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula:<BR><B>what about a briggs and stratton 1.5 HP high reving motor?  of course you feel like your driving a civic but you have a whole horse and a half of pavement eating, tire squeeling, Lawn Mower blowing, Adrenline rushing, POWER!!!!!!!! YEAH</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>If we wanted that we could of bought a Geo.<BR>; o )<P>||||reg||1
