Z||000018||HYPTNOTiSE||07-20-2000||06:52 PM||||I was in a pit crew for a late-model race car, which a dirt track stock car. He had a 40,000 dollar all aluminum brodix small block build by earl gaerte, and it was 430cid. it used a single dominator carb, and a dry sump system. It made like 700hp i think. You could put that in a fiero if you wanted. He has a spare engine for sale too, but i think he wants like 12-15 grand for it, but it doesn't run like the 40K one, it's still a 430 but it only makes like 600hp.<P>------------------<BR>Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ nitrous||||reg||1
